 After all chapters merge, a **full-book continuity audit** runs before final review. The auditor processes every chapter sequentially, building a cumulative world state and flagging long-range contradictions, unresolved plot threads, and accumulated drift that per-chapter checks can't catch. Results are compiled into `notes/continuity-audit-report.md`.
 
+### Release Phase
+
+Final review no longer ends the pipeline. It moves the project to `PACKAGING` and hands off to two release stages:
+
+1. **Package manuscript** — the packager assembles the merged chapters into `manuscript/manuscript.md` and writes a `release/manifest.json`. On success the project moves to `RELEASING`.
+2. **Generate listing** — the marketer writes the KDP store listing to `release/listing.json`. Reconcile validates it against the KDP rules (blurb length, exactly 7 keywords and 3 categories, allowed HTML, no unresolved placeholders) before marking the project `RELEASED`; a listing that fails validation marks the project `FAILED` instead.
+
